# Sisters Flowers — Permanent UI/UX Standards

All design and frontend development must follow these principles.

## Design direction
- Premium Da Lat flower studio digital extension matching SF orange brand materials (flyer/sign: bold burnt orange + black type)
- Brand tokens: Orange `#C24712`, Cream `#FFF4EB`, White `#FFFFFF`, Grey `#5C574F`, Wood `#B58B65`
- Orange must be unmistakable: header accent bar, brand wordmark, primary CTAs, prices, bot launcher, and intentional brand bands
- Cream/white still dominate catalog/product surfaces so bouquet photography sells first — do not paint every page solid orange
- Homepage may use a full orange brand band (like print materials); catalog/checkout stay calmer
- Avoid pastel pink/sage “field flower” gradients and generic template aesthetics

## Principles
1. **Mobile-first** — design for smartphones first; desktop equally polished
2. **Visual symmetry** — consistent spacing, alignment, card proportions, typography; use the spacing system, avoid arbitrary margins
3. **Comfort** — intuitive, calm, one-hand friendly; minimize unnecessary steps
4. **Professional** — consistent tokens, radii, components, iconography
5. **Responsive product grids** — prefer 2 columns on suitable mobile widths; consistent image aspect ratios; align titles/prices; prevent layout shift
6. **Touch-friendly** — aim for ≥44×44px targets; filters in a sheet on mobile, not half the screen
7. **Performance** — optimized images, lazy below-fold media, light animations; respect `prefers-reduced-motion`
8. **Accessibility** — readable type, contrast, focus states, accessible forms
9. **Language compatibility** — EN/VI (and future locales); layouts must tolerate longer Vietnamese strings
10. **Consistency across** homepage, catalog, product, custom bouquet, cart, checkout — without forcing identical card/block patterns everywhere (harmony ≠ sameness)

## Catalog specifics
- Featured occasions first; rest behind “All occasions”
- Prominent EN/VI search (accent-insensitive)
- Price presets + custom min/max
- Visible result counts; hide empty categories from chips
- Clean cards: photo → name → price → open (no card clutter)
- Subtle hover lift on desktop only; no heavy 3D/glass on every catalog card

## Effects policy
- Homepage / brand pages: stronger scroll/visual storytelling allowed
- Catalog & checkout: minimal motion
- Prefer CSS transforms/opacity over heavy WebGL unless a real product need (e.g. future 3D prints)

## Quality control
Test at 320, 375, 390, 430, 768, 1024, 1440px: alignment, wrapping, touch targets, image ratios, overflow, CLS.

## Stack constraints
Keep Prisma + SQLite until an explicit migration task. Do not change production secrets. Prefer Hostinger deploys for review.
